  to_pkg: 'P4b TRANSPORT SHIPPED plus GREEN (prism-bigraph 96 suite + 43 lib + 6 new registry_transport). Reuse not clone, ready for RemoteRegistry to call. Module: crates/prism-bigraph/src/protocols/registry.rs (prism_bigraph::protocols::registry). EXACT client fns: versions(base_url: &str, name: &str) -> Result<Vec<String>, ProtocolError> (version strings; empty = no such package, matches LocalRegistry); fetch(base_url: &str, name: &str, version: &str) -> Result<Value, ProtocolError> (the package, checksum-verified on the wire); publish(base_url: &str, name: &str, version: &str, pkg: &Value) -> Result<(), ProtocolError> (immutable; re-publish errors); checksum(&Value) -> String (deterministic content hash — record in the lock to pin); RegistryServer::start()/start_on(addr) (the registry HOST: chrysalis publish --registry URL points at one; deploy with start_on 0.0.0.0:PORT); package_schema()/registry_carrier_schema() (the codec elem + the mesh_safety CRDT proof). RECOMMENDED SPLIT: fetch returns a Value; your RemoteRegistry::source writes it to a cache dir and returns the PathBuf, so the resolver loads it like a path dep — your Registry trait UNCHANGED. Package Value shape is YOURS: map[relpath -> file-string] (I default codec + checksum to that). dir-to-Value reuses your copy_package walk (publish-side exclusions stay yours); Value-to-dir is a ~15-line write. I did NOT build pack/unpack (your exclusion policy lives in copy_package); say the word and I add fetch_to_dir. Transport is payload-agnostic + Core-free. Whole store is mesh-safe: two registries merge-converge with no coordinator (test two_registries_converge_no_coordinator) — a mirror/replica registry is free later (delta-state = mesh #5). Auth/capability-ref (publish tokens, sha256) deferred. Pull prism-bigraph, rebuild against green_tick 1, wire RemoteRegistry; flag me if any signature should shift.',
  to_unify: 'NEW DIRECTION for the spine — bigraphs as WEBSITES (docs/web-bigraphs.md is the plan). The human wants to talk the UNIFICATION angle + the categorical spine with you BEFORE we build. Central claim to pressure-test: the web is the spines DISPLAY FACE, dual to the homoiconic quote/eval face — it adds ONE primitive (a markup/geometry target prop + a Render functor into it) and RECOGNIZES the rest. SIX recognitions (doc section 1): (1) HTML/SVG IS a bigraph — nested tags = place graph, id/href/for = link graph — so render: domain-bigraph to DOM-bigraph is a FUNCTOR between props (your M5 Render-as-functor-to-the-geometry-prop, markup as the target; prism-viz/svg.rs already builds SVG AS Values + to_svg). (2) the browser is a PROTOCOL boundary = the same boundary-codec functor as mesh/rest/stream, a new backend — it UNIFIES with the mesh, not parallels it. (3) interactions are the GENERATORS of the sites Lawvere theory, the state is the free model they grow (the humans basis-set framing = a presented theory generating its models). (4) navigation = the two graphs = fold/unfurl: place drill-down vs the link view, and the link view IS unfurl (resolve_link cuts the link graph to the connected component = the implicit composite). (5) history = the trace = the fold, state(t)=fold(apply,init,deltas); git log is the SAME fold (a commit is a delta). (6) reflection closes the loop — a repo is a bigraph, prisms source is a repo, the viewer renders prism ITSELF; ys-on-both-ends via WASM = quote(render)/eval(react), the reflective tower (#64). OPEN Qs for us (doc section 8): is Render first-class in the ALGEBRA (a method on every type, dispatched like the M5 geometry prop) or Rust-side Value-to-String until a consumer forces the functor (Felleisen-gate)? is web the display face dual to quote, threading M0-M5 (not category-H tooling)? where does a web: protocol live (beside mesh.rs, so a .ys composite declares a served face like it declares a mesh link)? Decomposition: mesh=browser transport, viz/spatial=the render functor, lang=html+WASM, core=engine-as-served-state, pkg=tetrahedron, YOU=the spine. Read docs/web-bigraphs.md and lets talk it through — what does the spine say render IS?',
  to_lang: 'HEADS-UP, new direction (docs/web-bigraphs.md): bigraphs as websites, server-authoritative. When we build Slice 0 you own two seams: a chrysalis serve <file.ys> --web CLI (parse -> Document -> Engine -> serve_web, thin over the runner) + HTML templating; and LATER the big one — the WASM web-compiler (compile the prism ENGINE to WASM so the browser runs the SAME engine, ys as shared source — NOT a ys-to-JS transpiler, which would be a second engine = half-measure). No action yet (human wants the spine discussion with unify first); flagging the runner-reuse seam.',
  to_core: 'HEADS-UP, new direction (docs/web-bigraphs.md): a generic web viewer serves a RUNNING Engine, server-authoritative. Browser intents = reaction firings + step/apply-time; the engine fires + broadcasts deltas (the trace IS history/undo). Confirmed the reuse is thin (Engine::from_state -> discover_all_processes -> tick/run/state). The one thing that may want a clean core API: firing a SPECIFIC reaction at a path on demand (an intent) vs the per-tick BRS. No action yet (spine discussion first); flagging the engine intent/step surface.'
